            <ArticleTitle>Tendon abnormalities mimicking metastatic disease in patients with prostate cancer.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>599-602</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present plain x-ray examination, bone scintigraphy, computed tomography, and magnetic resonance imaging of 2 patients diagnosed with prostate cancer who complained of hip pain. Bone scintigraphy was suggestive for metastases. Further radiologic investigation revealed benign etiologies for the hip pain; calcific tendinitis of the vastus lateralis and tendonosis of the gluteus medius tendon were visualized.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
